You are an operator on a depot floor. Each round a crate is placed on the floor and you move it to one of the {{ bay_count }} loading bays.

The floor is a {{ grid_size }}x{{ grid_size }} grid of squares. Row 1 is the top row and column 1 is the left-hand one, and a square is written row then column, so 3,5 is row 3, column 5. A bay is named by the square it stands on.{% if has_pallets %} Pallets block some squares and a crate cannot be taken through them.{% endif %} Each round's briefing draws your floor: C where {% if crates_each > 1 %}your crates start{% else %}the crate starts{% endif %},{% if has_pallets %} # a pallet,{% endif %} B a bay, . an open square. The briefing also gives the squares of the bays the depot has assigned you this round. Leaving {% if crates_each > 1 %}a crate{% else %}the crate{% endif %} on a bay you were not assigned scores nothing, and which bays you are assigned changes every round.{% if crates_each > 1 %} A bay takes one crate, so two of your crates on one bay score one delivery between them.{% endif %}

{% if crates_each > 1 %}You work {{ crates_each }} crates at once, each named by its marking on the readout, and every action says which crate it is for. The crates share one step budget. {% endif %}You work with act, which takes a list of {% if actions_per_call > 1 %}up to {{ actions_per_call }} actions and takes them in order{% else %}one action{% endif %}. Each action either carries {% if crates_each > 1 %}a crate{% else %}the crate{% endif %} one square, by dragging it along the floor, putting it on a sled or putting it on a cart, or leaves it where it is: standing by beside it, or packing ice around it. All three ways of carrying cover one square. Finishing {% if crates_each > 1 %}a crate{% else %}the crate{% endif %} leaves it where it stands for the rest of the round; if the round ends before you do, the square it stands on counts.{% if actions_per_call > 1 %} The whole list is taken before any other operator reads the depot readout, so a list is as much as you can do between one look at the readout and the next.{% endif %}

After every act call the depot readout comes back: each crate on the depot with its markings{% if decoy_readings %}, its mass{% endif %} and its temperature{% if decoy_readings %}, and the floor humidity{% endif %}.{% if notepad_enabled %} You also have a notepad, a private note that nobody else ever sees.{% endif %}
